        "body": "🔥 METHOD 2: HORIZONTAL SCALING (DUPLICATION METHOD)\nMETHOD 2: HORIZONTAL SCALING\n\"Clone Winners Instead of Risking Originals\"\nPHASE 1: UNDERSTAND HORIZONTAL SCALING (Philosophy)\nCore Idea: Instead of raising budget on 1 winning ad set,\nDUPLICATE it multiple times at the SAME budget\nMultiple $50/day ad sets = safer than 1 × $500/day ad set\nWHY it works:\n• Each duplicate enters the auction INDEPENDENTLY\n• Facebook finds NEW users for each duplicate\n• Risk is spread — if 1 duplicate fails, others continue\n• Avoids algorithm disruption from large budget jumps\n• Lets you test small variations within duplicates\nPHASE 2: THE DUPLICATION STRUCTURE (Day 1)\nOriginal Winning Ad Set: $50/day (KEEP RUNNING — do not touch)\nCreate duplicates:\nOriginal : $50/day — Keep as-is (DO NOT EDIT)\nDuplicate 1 : $50/day — Exact copy, new launch\nDuplicate 2 : $50/day — Exact copy, different start time\nDuplicate 3 : $75/day — Same audience + higher budget\nDuplicate 4 : $50/day — Same creative, broader audience\nDuplicate 5 : $50/day — Same creative, different country\nTotal Daily Spend: $325/day (from original $50/day)\nPHASE 3: DUPLICATION VARIATIONS TO TEST (Day 1-3)\nEach duplicate can test ONE small variation:\nType What Changes Keep Same\nExact Clone Nothing — pure copy Everything\nBudget Variant Budget only (+50%) Everything\nAudience Variant Broader age range Creative\nPlacement Variant Feed only vs all placem. Audience\nCountry Variant UK/CA instead of USA Creative\nBid Variant Cost Cap instead of LC Audience\nPHASE 4: MANAGE DUPLICATE PORTFOLIO (Day 3-10)\nAfter 3–5 days, score each duplicate:\n✅ ROAS > target → Keep running + consider further duplicate\n✅ ROAS near target → Keep but don't scale yet\n❌ ROAS < 1.5× after 5 days → Pause and replace\n❌ CPA > 2× target after 5 days → Kill immediately\nGoal: Build a \"stable\" of 3–5 performing duplicates\nEach generating $50–$100/day in profit independently\nPHASE 5: HORIZONTAL + VERTICAL COMBO (Day 10-30)\nBest duplicates → now vertical scale (+20% every 48 hours)\nPoor duplicates → kill and replace with new duplicates\nContinuously duplicate the current BEST performer\nKeep original winner running unchanged — it is your \"control\"\nBEST FOR : ABO campaigns, risk-averse scaling\nBUDGET RANGE : $50–$500/day per duplicate\nRISK LEVEL : 🟢 LOW-MODERATE\nSPEED : Medium — can 5-10× spend in 2 weeks\nDIFFICULTY : ⭐⭐☆☆☆ (Beginner-Intermediate)\nIDEAL PHASE : Month 1–4 of scaling journey"
