        "title": "METHOD 5: COST CAP SCALING METHOD",
        "tagline": "Scale With A Profit Floor — Never Lose Control",
        "meta": {},
        "body": "🔥 METHOD 5: COST CAP SCALING METHOD\nMETHOD 5: COST CAP SCALING\n\"Scale With A Profit Floor — Never Lose Control\"\nPHASE 1: COST CAP SCALING FOUNDATION (Day 1-3)\nCost Cap = You set the MAXIMUM average CPA you'll accept\nFacebook only spends when it can hit your cap (or lower)\nThis lets you scale budget without scaling your CPA\nPre-Requisite: Know your profitable CPA\nProduct Selling Price : $49.99\nCOGS + Shipping : $18.00\nGross Profit : $31.99\nTarget Net Margin (40%) : $19.99\nMaximum Acceptable CPA : $31.99 - $19.99 = $12.00\nCost Cap Setting : $22–$28 (buffer added)\nPHASE 2: COST CAP LADDER SETUP (Day 3-5)\nRun 4 ad sets simultaneously with different Cost Cap levels:\nAd Set 1 : Cap $22 (aggressive) + $100/day budget\nAd Set 2 : Cap $25 (target) + $100/day budget\nAd Set 3 : Cap $28 (buffer) + $100/day budget\nAd Set 4 : Cap $32 (high) + $100/day budget\nObservation: Which cap level achieves full spend + best CPA?\nExpected Behavior:\n• $22 cap → Underspends (too restrictive for Facebook)\n• $25 cap → Partial spend (competitive sweet spot)\n• $28 cap → Full spend + CPA near $24–$26 (WINNER)\n• $32 cap → Full spend but CPA may approach $30\nPHASE 3: SCALE WINNING COST CAP (Day 5-14)\nWinning ad set (full spend + on-target CPA):\n✅ Increase budget ONLY (keep same cost cap number)\n✅ Budget increase: +30% every 48–72 hours\n✅ Cost Cap stays FIXED as you scale budget\n✅ This is the \"self-regulating\" power of Cost Cap scaling\nScaling Example (Cap fixed at $28):\nDay 5 : $100/day + $28 cap → CPA ~$26\nDay 8 : $130/day + $28 cap → CPA ~$26 (stable)\nDay 11 : $170/day + $28 cap → CPA ~$27\nDay 14 : $220/day + $28 cap → CPA ~$27 (still safe!)\nDay 17 : $285/day + $28 cap → Monitor closely\nDay 20 : $370/day + $28 cap → SCALE WINNER\nPHASE 4: COST CAP TROUBLESHOOTING (Common Issues)\nIssue: Campaign underspending at scale\nFix: Raise cost cap by $3–$5 increments until full spend\nIssue: CPA exceeds cost cap setting\nFix: Lower budget 20% — Facebook is struggling to find deals\nIssue: Inconsistent daily spend (some days high, some low)\nFix: Normal behavior — evaluate on 7-day rolling average\nIssue: Strong start then performance decay after 2 weeks\nFix: Creative refresh — add 3 new creatives to the ad set\nPHASE 5: ADVANCED COST CAP MANAGEMENT (Day 14+)\nRun Cost Cap alongside Lowest Cost for comparison\nDuring Q4/peak season: Raise cap 15% to stay competitive\nDuring slow periods: Lower cap 10% to maintain efficiency\nUse Cost Cap for scaling + Lowest Cost for prospecting\nBuild \"cap portfolio\": Multiple ad sets at different caps\nBEST FOR : Sellers who need strict CPA control at scale\nBUDGET RANGE : $100–$3,000+/day\nRISK LEVEL : 🟢 LOW (CPA protected by design)\nSPEED : Moderate — self-regulating\nDIFFICULTY : ⭐⭐⭐⭐☆ (Advanced)\nIDEAL PHASE : Month 3+ when you know your target CPA"
