        "body": "🔥 METHOD 6: CREATIVE SCALING METHOD\nMETHOD 6: CREATIVE SCALING\n\"More Winning Creatives = More Scale Capacity\"\nPHASE 1: THE CREATIVE SCALING PHILOSOPHY (Foundation)\nTruth: Budget scaling is LIMITED by creative fatigue\nReality: Most campaigns fail to scale due to creative burnout\nSolution: Scale your CREATIVE VOLUME to enable budget scale\nFormula: More winning creatives = higher budget ceiling\nCreative Scaling Equation:\n1 winning creative → max $200–$500/day sustainable\n3 winning creatives → max $500–$1,500/day sustainable\n6 winning creatives → max $1,500–$5,000/day sustainable\n10+ winning creatives → $5,000–$20,000+/day possible\nPHASE 2: BUILD YOUR CREATIVE PIPELINE (Day 1-7)\nWeekly Creative Production System:\nMONDAY : Brief 4 new creatives (concepts defined)\nTUESDAY : Send briefs to creators/editors\nWEDNESDAY : Review and approve drafts\nTHURSDAY : Final edits + upload to ad account\nFRIDAY : Launch new creatives in test structure\nWEEKEND : Review performance of previous week's tests\nMinimum: 4 new creatives per week at scaling phase\nAggressive: 8–12 new creatives per week at high scale\nPHASE 3: CREATIVE ITERATION FRAMEWORK (Day 7-14)\nTake every winning creative and iterate systematically:\nWinning Creative: \"UGC video — woman finds ants, uses guide\"\nIteration 1: Same video + different hook (first 3 secs)\nIteration 2: Same video + different text overlay color\nIteration 3: Same video + new CTA at end\nIteration 4: Shorter cut (45sec → 22sec version)\nIteration 5: Same angle — different creator (male)\nIteration 6: Square format instead of vertical\nIteration 7: Add captions/subtitles to existing video\nIteration 8: Different background music track\n1 winning creative → 8 iterations → 2–3 new winners likely\nPHASE 4: CREATIVE FATIGUE MONITORING (Ongoing)\nCreative Fatigue Warning Signs:\nSignal Threshold Action\nFrequency > 3.0 in 7 days Refresh creative\nCTR Drop -30% from peak Replace creative\nCPA Increase +25% from avg Audit creatives\nROAS Drop -0.5× from avg New creative set\nCPM Spike +40% sudden Audience saturat\nPHASE 5: CREATIVE SCALING CONTENT TYPES (Prioritized)\nRank creative types by scaling longevity (highest to lowest):\n🥇 Rank 1: UGC testimonial videos (longest fatigue resistance\n🥈 Rank 2: Problem/solution narrative videos\n🥉 Rank 3: Before/after transformation content\n4th: Static lifestyle images (fade fastest at high spend)\n5th: Carousel formats (good for retargeting, weak for cold)\n6th: Single static product-only images (fastest fatigue)\nBEST FOR : Any seller who wants to break scaling ceilings\nBUDGET RANGE : Applies at every budget level\nRISK LEVEL : 🟢 LOW (investment in assets, not blind spend)\nSPEED : Compounds over time — faster as library grows\nDIFFICULTY : ⭐⭐⭐☆☆ (Intermediate)\nIDEAL PHASE : Start from Day 1 — never stop creative testing"
