        "body": "🔥 METHOD 8: INTERNATIONAL MARKET SCALING\nMETHOD 8: INTERNATIONAL MARKET SCALING\n\"When USA Gets Expensive — The World Opens Up\"\nPHASE 1: INTERNATIONAL EXPANSION READINESS CHECK (Day 1)\nBefore expanding internationally, confirm:\n✅ USA campaign is profitable (ROAS > 2.5×)\n✅ Shopify store accepts international payments\n✅ Shipping to target countries is available + priced\n✅ Product page works in target country language\n✅ Currency display set up correctly on store\n✅ Return/refund policy covers international customers\n✅ Tax/VAT compliance reviewed (esp. UK, EU, AU)\nPHASE 2: MARKET TIER EXPANSION ORDER (Day 1-3)\nExpand in this order (risk-managed sequence):\nWAVE 1 (Month 1–2): English-Speaking Tier 1\n→ UK : $50/day — high similarity to USA\n→ CA : $40/day — almost identical buying behavior\n→ AU : $40/day — English, high income, high CPM\n→ NZ : $20/day — small market, high quality\nWAVE 2 (Month 2–3): Western Europe (if product fits)\n→ DE : $40/day — translate ad copy\n→ NL : $30/day — high English fluency\n→ SE : $30/day — strong e-commerce market\n→ NO : $25/day — high disposable income\nWAVE 3 (Month 3+): Emerging Markets\n→ ZA : $20/day — low CPM, moderate buying power\n→ PH : $15/day — very low CPM, volume market\n→ MX : $20/day — large market, price-sensitive\nPHASE 3: INTERNATIONAL CAMPAIGN STRUCTURE (Day 3-7)\nStructure options for international campaigns:\nOption A: One Country Per Campaign (Most Control)\n→ Separate ABO per country\n→ Full budget + creative control per market\n→ Best for: UK and DE (high-value, worth individual attention)\nOption B: Region Bundle (Efficiency)\n→ \"CA + AU + NZ\" in one ad set\n→ \"DE + NL + SE\" in one ad set\n→ Good when budget is limited\nOption C: Worldwide ASC (Autopilot)\n→ One ASC targeting all countries\n→ Facebook allocates budget to best-performing markets\n→ Least control but maximum reach\nPHASE 4: LOCALIZATION FOR SCALE (Day 7-14)\nBasic localization (doubles conversion rate in non-USA):\nUK : Change $ to £, use UK spelling, UK testimonials\nCA : CAD pricing, French option for Quebec\nAU : AUD pricing, local delivery times, AU slang\nDE : Full German translation of ads + landing page\nALL : Local currency display on Shopify\nALL : Country-specific shipping ETA in ad copy\nPHASE 5: INTERNATIONAL PORTFOLIO MANAGEMENT (Ongoing)\nTrack each country's MER independently\nScale winners: +20% budget every 48hrs for profitable markets\nKill losers: Any market with CPA > 2× target after 14 days\nSeasonal calendar: Different peak seasons per country\nTarget revenue mix: USA 50% + UK 20% + CA/AU 20% + Other 10%\nBEST FOR : Reducing CPA dependence on USA market\nBUDGET RANGE : $150–$500/day across all international markets\nRISK LEVEL : 🟡 MODERATE (compliance + logistics risk)\nSPEED : Medium — 4–8 weeks to stabilize each market\nDIFFICULTY : ⭐⭐⭐⭐☆ (Advanced)\nIDEAL PHASE : Month 3+ after USA campaigns are profitable"
