        "body": "🔥 METHOD 12: DAYPARTING & BUDGET SCHEDULING SCALE\nMETHOD 12: DAYPARTING SCALING\n\"Spend Your Budget When Buyers Are Most Active\"\nPHASE 1: DAYPARTING DATA ANALYSIS (Day 1-7)\nFirst: Collect 14–30 days of campaign performance data\nIn Ads Manager: Breakdown → Time → Hour of Day\nIn Ads Manager: Breakdown → Time → Day of Week\nCreate your own performance heatmap:\nTypical High-Performance Windows (e-commerce):\nHOUR OF DAY (EST):\n12AM–2AM : 🔴 Low (night owls — low intent)\n6AM–8AM : 🟡 Med (commute browsing)\n8AM–11AM : 🟢 HIGH (morning intent peak)\n11AM–1PM : 🟢 HIGH (lunch break shopping)\n1PM–5PM : 🟡 Med (work hours — lower attention)\n5PM–9PM : 🟢 PEAK (evening prime time — BEST)\n9PM–12AM : 🟢 HIGH (relaxed evening browsing)\nDAY OF WEEK:\nMonday : 🟡 Medium — post-weekend\nTuesday : 🟢 HIGH — strong buying intent\nWednesday : 🟢 HIGH — midweek impulse buying\nThursday : 🟢 HIGH — pre-weekend planning\nFriday : 🟢 PEAK — payday + weekend mood\nSaturday : 🟡 Medium — varied (leisure vs shopping)\nSunday : 🟡 Medium — relaxed but moderate intent\nPHASE 2: BUILD CUSTOM PERFORMANCE HEATMAP (Day 7-10)\nPull YOUR account's actual data (not generic benchmarks)\nScore each time block on ROAS or CPA:\nHour Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun\n6am B B B B B A A\n9am B A A A A B B\n12pm A A A+ A A B A\n3pm C B B B A B B\n6pm A+ A+ A+ A+ A+ A A\n9pm A A A A+ A+ A+ A\nA+ = Best ROAS | A = Good | B = Average | C = Poor\nPHASE 3: IMPLEMENT DAYPARTING SCHEDULE (Day 10-14)\nApply scheduling in Facebook Ads Manager:\nCampaign → Ad Set → Budget & Schedule → Run on a Schedule\nBudget Scheduling Strategy:\n\"A+\" time blocks → Run at 130% of normal budget\n\"A\" time blocks → Run at 100% of normal budget\n\"B\" time blocks → Run at 70% of normal budget\n\"C\" time blocks → Pause entirely (save budget)\nNet result: Same total spend — deployed more efficiently\nPHASE 4: WEEKEND vs WEEKDAY BUDGET SPLIT (Day 14-21)\nCreate 2 identical campaigns:\nCampaign A: Scheduled weekdays only (higher budget)\nCampaign B: Scheduled weekends only (different budget)\nCompare ROAS separately → allocate more to winner\nFriday Scale-Up Tactic:\nEvery Thursday night: Increase budget +25% for Friday-Sunday\nEvery Monday morning: Return to baseline budget\nPHASE 5: SEASONAL DAYPARTING ADJUSTMENT (Ongoing)\nSummer (pest season): Increase AM budgets (early pest sighti )\nWinter (rodent season): Increase evening budgets\nPayday weeks (1st/15th): Increase budgets across all slots\nQ4 (Oct–Dec): Expand time windows — buyers active more hours\nBEST FOR : Optimizing efficiency of existing campaigns\nBUDGET RANGE : Any — efficiency play not spend play\nRISK LEVEL : 🟢 LOW (no new spend — better allocation)\nSPEED : Immediate efficiency gain within 1 week\nDIFFICULTY : ⭐⭐⭐☆☆ (Intermediate)\nIDEAL PHASE : Month 2+ when you have 30 days of data"
