        "meta": {},
        "body": "🔥 METHOD 14: MULTI-PRODUCT LINE SCALING\nMETHOD 14: MULTI-PRODUCT LINE SCALING\n\"Scale Revenue By Expanding What You Sell\"\nPHASE 1: PRODUCT LINE EXPANSION STRATEGY (Day 1-7)\nThe Revenue Ceiling Problem:\n• One product → audience saturates → CPA rises → scale stops\n• Solution: Multiple products = multiple audiences + revenue\n• Cross-sell existing buyers → highest ROAS possible\nProduct Expansion Map (Pest Control Example):\nHERO PRODUCT (Current)\n→ Ant Control PDF Guide ($19.99)\nEXPANSION TIER 1 (Month 2–3) — Adjacent Products\n→ Cockroach Elimination Guide ($19.99)\n→ Mouse & Rat Control Guide ($19.99)\n→ Bed Bug Battle Guide ($19.99)\nEXPANSION TIER 2 (Month 3–4) — Premium Products\n→ \"Complete Home Pest Defense\" Mega Bundle ($49.99)\n→ Seasonal Pest Prevention System ($34.99)\n→ Natural Remedy Kit Bundle ($59.99)\nEXPANSION TIER 3 (Month 4–6) — High Ticket\n→ Online Pest Control Masterclass ($97–$197)\n→ Annual Pest Defense Membership ($9.99/month)\n→ Property Manager License Pack ($299)\nPHASE 2: MULTI-PRODUCT AD CAMPAIGN STRUCTURE (Day 7-14)\nAs new products launch → add new campaigns:\nCampaign 1: Hero Product (Ant Guide) — $100/day\nCampaign 2: New Product (Roach Guide) — $50/day test\nCampaign 3: Bundle Offer — $75/day\nCampaign 4: Retargeting all products — $50/day\nCampaign 5: Post-purchase upsells — $30/day\nTotal: $305/day across growing product catalog\nEach new product = New advertising angle + new audience access\nPHASE 3: CROSS-SELL CAMPAIGN SCALING (Day 14-21)\nBuild dedicated cross-sell campaigns:\nAudience: Past buyers of Product A\nOffer: \"You solved ants — do you have roaches too?\"\nBudget: $20–$40/day per cross-sell campaign\nExpected ROAS: 5–10× (warm audience = cheap conversions)\nCross-Sell Matrix:\nBought Ant Guide → Offer Roach Guide (60% take rate)\nBought Roach Guide → Offer Complete Bundle (45% take)\nBought Any Guide → Offer Natural Kit (35% take)\nBought Bundle → Offer Membership (25% take)\nPHASE 4: CATALOG SCALING WITH DYNAMIC ADS (Day 21-30)\nAs product catalog grows (5+ products):\nSet up Facebook Product Catalog\nEnable Dynamic Ads → shows RIGHT product to right person\nFacebook automatically tests which product each person buys\nThis replaces manual campaign management at scale\nPHASE 5: BRAND PORTFOLIO SCALING (Month 3+)\nRevenue distribution target at scale:\nIndividual guides (5–8 products) : 30% of revenue\nBundle products (2–3 bundles) : 35% of revenue\nPhysical kits (1–2 SKUs) : 20% of revenue\nMembership/subscription : 15% of revenue\nThis diversification = stable scaling foundation\nBEST FOR : Breaking through single-product scaling ceiling\nBUDGET RANGE : Increases proportionally with product catalog\nRISK LEVEL : 🟡 MODERATE (new product development required)\nSPEED : Medium — 4–8 weeks per new product launch\nDIFFICULTY : ⭐⭐⭐⭐☆ (Advanced)\nIDEAL PHASE : Month 3+ after hero product is proven"
